Chapter~\ref{ch:background} establishes the shared concepts and compares related work according to evidence representation, retrieval, updates, matching, and context serving. It includes the hyper-relational study as an information-preservation perspective. Chapters~\ref{ch:kglink}--\ref{ch:mgrag} then develop the four research questions in sequence. Each chapter gives its problem, method, evaluation protocol, published evidence, and discussion.

Chapter~\ref{ch:discussion} compares the points at which structure enters these pipelines. It examines static and query-dependent evidence, the relationship between quality and computational cost, and the conditions affecting interpretation. Chapter~\ref{ch:conclusion} returns to the research questions and identifies directions for future work. The organization brings the studies together through their evidence interfaces while preserving the particular task and protocol through which each contribution was evaluated.

